    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d529">

                <pb facs="0812" n="794" sameAs="frus:frus1946v05/pg794"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Germany)/1–246: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the United States Political Adviser for Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Murphy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-01-02T17:00:00-05:00">January 2, 1946—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2. It will soon be four months since Control Council passed its resolution<anchor
                        n="19" xml:id="d529-f1"/> regarding recall of German officials, agents and
                    obnoxious persons from neutral countries. Information reaching Dept indicates
                    that compliance has been complete in Afghanistan, moderately satisfactory in
                    Sweden, partial in Switzerland and negligible in Spain, Portugal, Ireland and
                    the Vatican. It is to be borne in mind, however, that Spanish Govt at least can
                    allege that no actual facilities for repatriation of Germans have been
                    offered.</p>
                <p>Consider in connection with this problem Bern’s 4919, Dec. 4 to Dept repeated to
                    you as 89; Lisbon’s 2329 Dec 4 to Dept repeated to you; Amvat 225, Nov 21, to Dept repeated to you;
                    Madrid’s 2363, Nov 21 repeated to you as 40; Madrid’s 2428, Nov 30 repeated to
                    you as 69; Madrid’s despatch no. 1176, Nov 15 copy of which was sent you; and
                    Madrid’s despatch 1140 Nov 10 copy of which was sent you.<anchor n="20"
                        xml:id="d529-f2"/> Dublin does not appear to have repeated relevant
                    telegrams to you but has been unable to elicit from Eire Govt any indication of
                    cooperation in this matter.</p>
                <p>Jan 10 may be appropriate date for some statement by Control Council preparatory
                    to subsequent efforts to arouse world opinion in behalf of repatriation of
                    obnoxious Germans from neutral states. Please consult your colleagues informally
                    in this sense and unless your and their reactions are negative initiate action
                    in this sense.</p>
                <p>Repeated to London as Dept’s 8.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
